&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Senior Site Due Diligence Design Engineer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About the Team&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Senior Site Due Diligence Design Engineer plays a critical role in CoreWeave&#39;s data centre development pipeline by providing the first full technical evaluation of prospective sites. As the first engineering representative in site selection and due diligence, you will bring a broad, multidisciplinary perspective to judge how well each site can support CoreWeave&#39;s requirements across all major design disciplines.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will be the technical bridge between the Site Selection team and the broader Design &amp;amp; Engineering organisation. From first site introduction through lease execution or acquisition, you will lead technical due diligence. That includes evaluating infrastructure capacity, utility availability, building suitability, land use and entitlements, and early design constraints, and working directly with data centre providers, utilities, landlords, and external partners. Once a site is secured, you will hand it off to the assigned Design Manager for full project design. The role calls for strong engineering judgment, the ability to interpret information across disciplines, and the confidence to represent CoreWeave&#39;s technical priorities in early strategic conversations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role requires frequent travel to prospective data centre locations across the EMEA and APAC regions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Key Responsibilities:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Initial Technical Evaluation:&lt;/strong&gt; Act as the first technical evaluator for prospective data centre sites across electrical, mechanical, architectural, civil, and IT/LV disciplines, identifying technical risks, constraints, opportunities, and required upgrades.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Early-Phase Design Leadership:&lt;/strong&gt; Lead the design team from initial site concept through lease execution or acquisition, coordinating all design activities in these early phases. Take part in early design and scoping discussions to align everyone on CoreWeave&#39;s requirements and technical expectations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Proposal &amp;amp; Document Review:&lt;/strong&gt; Review provider proposals, capacity offers, utility information, conceptual layouts, and as-built drawings to confirm they align with CoreWeave&#39;s design principles. Make sure technical requirements are correctly reflected in early documents such as LOIs, provider proposals, and preliminary agreements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;External Engagement:&lt;/strong&gt; Work directly with landlords, developers, data centre providers, and utilities during early due diligence. Run early technical workshops with providers so they correctly understand CoreWeave&#39;s design expectations and project objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Power &amp;amp; Utility Assessment:&lt;/strong&gt; Review site infrastructure, including power availability, redundancy options, upstream utility constraints, delivery timelines, and required upgrades.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mechanical Feasibility:&lt;/strong&gt; Assess heat rejection options, water availability and quality, mechanical yard capacity, and compatibility with CoreWeave cooling strategies (e.g., chilled water plants, CDUs, TCS loops).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Building Suitability:&lt;/strong&gt; Evaluate structural capacity, floor loading, egress paths, ceiling heights, roof strength, envelope condition, and potential for expansion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Land Use &amp;amp; Entitlements:&lt;/strong&gt; Evaluate land use, zoning, permitting, and entitlement feasibility at a high level, and identify regulatory constraints or municipal approval risks that could affect schedule, density, or constructability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Conceptual MEP &amp;amp; Risk Assessment:&lt;/strong&gt; Develop high-level conceptual MEP assessments. Identify and document site-specific blockers and risks, with clear impacts on scope, cost, schedule, density, constructability, and long-term scalability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Assessments &amp;amp; Recommendations:&lt;/strong&gt; Prepare concise technical due diligence summaries and early go/no-go recommendations covering feasibility findings, required upgrades, regulatory considerations, and alignment with CoreWeave&#39;s design and operational requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pipeline Tracking:&lt;/strong&gt; Build and manage dashboards or similar tools to track technical progress, risks, land-use considerations, and milestones for all active candidate sites.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SME Collaboration:&lt;/strong&gt; Work with internal SMEs and the broader design team. Resolve early-stage questions yourself where possible, and route discipline-specific topics quickly to the right experts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Design Handover:&lt;/strong&gt; Deliver a structured technical handover to the assigned Design Manager once a lease is executed or a site is acquired, so full project design continues seamlessly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Qualifications:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of experience in data centre engineering, MEP consulting, site selection, due diligence, or early-phase design and development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Mechanical, Electrical, Civil, or Architectural Engineering, or equivalent relevant experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Broad technical competency across electrical, mechanical, civil/structural, and architectural fundamentals, with the ability to evaluate multi-discipline issues without full SME support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of utility infrastructure, such as power delivery, substations, feeders, water sources, and permitting, and how it affects site feasibility.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience reviewing capacity offers, conceptual site plans, utility data, and building documentation from data centre providers or developers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with land use, zoning, and entitlement processes, and the ability to identify regulatory risks that may affect feasibility or schedule.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with or exposure to data centre design standards, including cooling strategies, power distribution, redundancy concepts, and scalability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to turn complex technical information into clear written assessments and concise go/no-go recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to work independently during early assessments and exercise sound engineering judgment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong interpersonal skills, with experience engaging landlords, utilities, developers, and real estate teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication, technical writing, and presentation skills, including briefing leadership and cross-functional teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High comfort operating in a fast-paced, dynamic environment where rapid technical vetting and decision support are essential.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability and willingness to travel extensively to prospective data centre locations across EMEA and APAC.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Why CoreWeave?&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At CoreWeave, we work hard, have fun, and move fast! We&#39;re in an exciting stage of hyper-growth that you will not want to miss out on. We&#39;re not afraid of a little chaos, and we&#39;re constantly learning. Our team cares deeply about how we build our product and how we work together, which is represented through our core values:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be Curious at Your Core&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act Like an Owner&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Empower Employees&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver Best-in-Class Client Experiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Achieve More Together&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We support and encourage an entrepreneurial outlook and independent thinking. We foster an environment that encourages collaboration and enables the development of innovative solutions to complex problems. As we get set for takeoff, the organisation&#39;s growth opportunities are constantly expanding. You will be surrounded by some of the best talent in the industry, who will want to learn from you, too. Come join us!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Compensation &amp;amp; Benefits&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The starting salary will be determined by job-related knowledge, skills, experience, and the market location. We strive for both market alignment and internal equity when determining compensation. In addition to base salary, our total rewards package includes a discretionary bonus, equity awards, and a comprehensive benefits program (all based on eligibility).&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;To fulfill our obligation to protect client data, successful applicants offered employment with CoreWeave will be required to complete a basic criminal record check, conducted in compliance with GDPR. Employment offers are conditional upon receiving satisfactory check results.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In addition to a competitive salary, we offer a variety of benefits to support your needs, including:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Family-level Medical Insurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Family-level Dental Insurance&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous Pension Contribution&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Life Assurance at 4x Salary&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Critical Illness Cover&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Employee Assistance Programme&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tuition Reimbursement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work culture focused on innovative disruption&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Benefits may vary by location.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equal Opportunity&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;CoreWeave is an equal opportunity employer, committed to fostering an inclusive and supportive workplace. All qualified applicants and candidates will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, disability, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Recruitment Agencies&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;em data-stringify-type=&quot;italic&quot;&gt;CoreWeave does not accept speculative CVs. Any unsolicited CVs received will be treated as the property of CoreWeave and your Terms &amp;amp; Conditions associated with the use of CVs will be considered null and void.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;em data-stringify-type=&quot;italic&quot;&gt;Any unsolicited CVs sent by your company to us – that is to say, in any situation where we have not directly engaged your company in writing to supply candidates for a specific vacancy – will be considered by us to be a “free gift”, leaving us liable for no fees whatsoever should we choose to contact the candidate directly and engage the candidate’s services, and will in no way establish any prior claim by your company to representation of that candidate should the candidate’s details also be submitted by any other party.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Export Control Compliance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;This position requires access to technology and/or source code subject to U.S. export control laws. Any such access will be provided only in compliance with applicable U.S. export control requirements. As part of the recruitment process, CoreWeave may request limited information reasonably necessary to assess applicable export-control requirements.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Updated privacy notice - UK and EU Job Applications&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;When you apply to a job on this site, the personal data contained in your application will be collected by CoreWeave UK Ltd. (“Controller”), which is located at&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Phosphor (6th Floor), 133 Park Street, London, SE1 9EA&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;and can be contacted by emailing ----- Controller’s data protection officer can be contacted at ----- Your personal data will be processed for the purposes of managing Controller’s recruitment related activities, which include setting up and conducting interviews and tests for applicants, evaluating and assessing the results thereto, and as is otherwise needed in the recruitment and hiring processes. Such processing is legally permissible under Art. 6(1)(f) of (i) Regulation (EU) 2016/679 (General Data Protection Regulation (“GDPR”) and (ii) the GDPR as it forms part of the laws of the UK (“UK GDPR”), as necessary for the purposes of the legitimate interests pursued by the Controller, which are the solicitation, evaluation, and selection of applicants for employment. Your personal data will be shared with Greenhouse Software, Inc., a cloud services provider located in the United States of America and engaged by Controller to help manage its recruitment and hiring process on Controller’s behalf. With respect to transfers originating from the UK or the European Economic Area (&quot;EEA&quot;) to a country outside the UK or the EEA, we implement the appropriate transfer mechanism(s) and other appropriate solutions to address cross-border transfers as required by applicable law. You may request a copy of the suitable mechanisms we have in place by contacting us at &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a ----------
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Your personal data will be retained by Controller as long as Controller determines it is necessary to evaluate your application for employment. Where permitted by applicable law, we may also retain your personal data for a limited period after the recruitment process ends in order to consider you for future job opportunities, respond to legal claims, or comply with record-keeping obligations. Under the GDPR and the UK GDPR, you have the right to request access to your personal data, to request that your personal data be rectified or erased, and to request that processing of your personal data be restricted. You also have the right to data portability. In addition, you may lodge a complaint with the relevant supervisory authority: (i) A list of Europe’s data protection authorities can be found &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://urldefense.com/v3/__https://ec.europa.eu/justice/article-29/structure/data-protection-authorities/index_en.htm__;!!I6uDfDBXfA!zaqvpaXitCAqve4cpmPGknjMlTsgIw8w_6xTVeiRpNP5Eo6Ajz9ZkXAYM2uL-nlD8kD6Ndd-Oe-k_BEQQh9xVQGfFw$&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;here&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt;; and (ii) for the UK, this is the &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://urldefense.com/v3/__https://ico.org.uk/__;!!I6uDfDBXfA!zaqvpaXitCAqve4cpmPGknjMlTsgIw8w_6xTVeiRpNP5Eo6Ajz9ZkXAYM2uL-nlD8kD6Ndd-Oe-k_BEQQh9IDhJOUA$&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Information Commissioner&#39;s Office&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;For additional information, please see our &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.coreweave.com/docs/policies/terms-of-service/privacy-policy&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Privacy Policy&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Senior Operations and Planning Principal&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location&lt;/strong&gt;: London&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dept&lt;/strong&gt;: Business assistance&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Every business is using AI. The ones that get it right start with real people. GWI is the human intelligence underneath: verified data that helps businesses understand what moves their audience, and act on it faster. If you want your work to matter, keep reading.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;br&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;What will I be doing?&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As our Senior Operations and Planning Principal,&amp;nbsp; you’ll turn GWI’s vision and strategy into a plan the whole business can deliver, and make sure it happens. Reporting to the CFOO, you’ll work alongside the CEO, Founder and ELT as a trusted adviser and challenger: shaping priorities, testing trade-offs and keeping the leadership team aligned on what comes first and what doesn’t. This role is needed to take the strategy and vision into execution.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;br&gt;This is a senior, individual contributor level role with a seat in ELT discussions. You’ll own cross functional initiatives directly and run the operating rhythm that keeps the ELT moving, so that decisions are made, recorded and followed through. You’ll directly lead selected strategic initiatives and coordinate the wider transformation programme, ensuring accountable leaders have clear outcomes, dependencies and decisions to resolve.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A few things you’ll be responsible for:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translating company strategy into clear priorities, owned initiatives and a plan, each with an outcome, an owner and a deadline&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advising and challenging the ELT: bringing analysis, options and a recommendation to key decisions, and pressure testing priorities, resourcing and trade offs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leading cross-functional initiatives and the transformation programme, tracking outcomes rather than activity and raising risks early with a proposed way forward&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Running the ELT operating rhythm, including planning cycles, quarterly priority reviews and decision forums, with decisions documented and acted on&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Preparing decision papers and briefings for the CFOO, CEO, ELT, VP People &amp;amp; Talent, and representing the CFOO in cross-functional forums where needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mapping complex cross-functional problems, bringing the right people together and driving them to a decision&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communication of changing priorities&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Working at GWI means a high tempo environment where change is common. We’re building quickly because the industry is moving quickly, and our customers rely on us to stay ahead. If you like being part of that, you’ll enjoy it here.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;br&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;What do I need to bring with me?&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll need to be able to demonstrate the core skills this role requires. You don&#39;t have to tick all the boxes right away; the important thing is that you’re willing to learn.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven senior experience in strategy, consulting, business operations, ideally in a scaling tech business&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of turning strategy into an executable plan and delivering complex, cross-functional programmes to deadline&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong strategic judgement and commercial and financial fluency, with the analytical instinct to ask the right questions and quickly see what matters&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;across a leadership team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Builds trust and alignment with the right stakeholders and communicates ideas clearly and confidently to gain buy-in and move work forward, focussing on outcomes that deliver the greatest impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Credibility and confidence to challenge senior leaders constructively and persistently, including when it’s uncomfortable&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to turn a messy discussion into a clear, decision-ready paper people will actually read&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High emotional intelligence and the ability to influence without authority, up, down and&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort with ambiguity: you create clarity rather than wait for it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We actively encourage applications from underrepresented and marginalised communities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At GWI, you&#39;ll find a place to contribute meaningfully, grow professionally, and belong fully.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;Some benefits, to name a few! 🫶&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;25 days annual leave, December office closure, and early Friday finishes (1pm during summer)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;BUPA private medical insurance&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexitime &amp;amp; hybrid working&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enhanced parental leave: 26 weeks at 100% pay for primary caregivers, 8 weeks for co-caregivers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
