&lt;p&gt;Rithum is an equal opportunity employer. We are committed to providing an environment of mutual respect where equal employment opportunities are available to all applicants and teammates without regard to race, religion, color, sex, gender identity, sexual orientation, age, non-disqualifying physical or mental disability, national origin, veteran status or any other protected characteristic. All employment is decided on the basis of qualifications, merit, and business need.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re committed to providing reasonable accommodations in accordance with the law for qualified applicants. If you require assistance during the interview process due to a medical condition or need support accessing our website or completing the application process, please reach out to us by completing the &lt;a class=&quot;notion-link-token notion-focusable-token notion-enable-hover&quot; href=&quot;https://forms.office.com/r/v1qDcUpHLw&quot; data-token-index=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;link-annotation-unknown-block-id-248713042&quot;&gt;Accommodations Request Form&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;. Your comfort and accessibility are important to us, and we&#39;re here to ensure a seamless experience as you explore opportunities with our team.&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Company Profile&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;nLighten is a European platform of distributed edge data centers, designed to meet the growing demand for AI, 5G, and hybrid cloud deployments. As a rapidly expanding provider, we offer scalable colocation hubs and best-in-class energy solutions across Europe. Our innovative and sustainable approach to digital infrastructure ensures reliability, efficiency, and future-ready solutions for our clients. nLighten’s current footprint is 34 data centers in 7 European countries, with the ambition to grow to 100 sites during the next 3-4 years.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Learn more about us: &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.nlighten.com&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;www.nlighten.com&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking an &lt;strong&gt;Regional Compliance Senior Manager&lt;/strong&gt; to lead and optimize the operational performance of our data centers in the UK. In this role, you will be working on a 70-30 model. Wherein 70% of your responsibility will be to support your region maintain compliance to nLighten policies and to relevant Operational regulation (including but not limited to Environment, Health &amp;amp; Safety, Security, Data Privacy). While 30% of your role will be involved in managing nLighten level compliance projects given you a holistic view of the compliance footprint and ability to make a difference at a global company level. You will play a key role in shaping the future of our compliance as we expand our footprint. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead compliance effort of multiple data centers across UK ensuring high level of policy and regulatory adherence on continuous basis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a subject matter expert for topics related to EHS (Environment, Health &amp;amp; Safety) for nLighten.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and manage compliance projects at nLighten level (including but not limited to; process/policy definition and rollout, compliance training, KPI definition and tracking, etc.).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Closely track audit findings for the region and work with relevant stakeholders to encourage timely closure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform planned and adhoc internal checks/audits on various operational subjects including EHS, Security and Business Continuity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform need based and regular compliance training for in scope staff.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform EHS incident investigations and enable the team to identify root cause and remedial action.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee energy and environment compliance effort for the region and in certain cases for nLighten.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with leadership and cross-functional teams to align regional compliance with business strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Play a key role in scaling compliance maturity to support the company’s ambitious growth plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform cross-region internal audits as planned.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enforce the nLighten Safe-to-Work process (PPM, RAMS, MOP, Change Request, Permit to Work) at every site.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide guidance to regional Operations on EHS and any other compliance related budget plan.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support with external audits as a SME (Subject Matter Expert) for EHS and other compliance related topics. This includes certification and/or customer audits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with the wider compliance team to deliver a standard approach and overall improvement strategy for compliance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Performance Metrics&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Audit Finding Closure with Target timeline:&lt;/strong&gt; Maintaining high compliance status across all managed datacentres.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Subject Matter Expertise:&lt;/strong&gt; Managing queries relevant to EHS for nLighten and for the datacentres in scope.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Coaching:&lt;/strong&gt; Growth and performance of site technicians and regional managers on compliance topics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Process Improvements:&lt;/strong&gt; Identification and definition of new governance and compliance frameworks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Training and Rollout Management: &lt;/strong&gt;Enable site Ops to comply with all key processes and maintain a safe and secure working environment&lt;strong&gt;.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Customer:&lt;/strong&gt; Support with compliance related audits and customer queries across the region.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We’re Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;5+ years of experience in environmental, health, and safety programs &lt;/strong&gt;in a datacentre or a manufacturing or construction environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sound knowledge of &lt;strong&gt;safety standards and regulations in the UK&lt;/strong&gt;, sustainability best practices, and ISO 14001 and 45001 certification requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience of &lt;strong&gt;performing internal audits&lt;/strong&gt; OR qualification as a Lead Auditor.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Certification in &lt;strong&gt;NEBOSH, ASP, or CSP&lt;/strong&gt; is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Datacentre experience&lt;/strong&gt; is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with &lt;strong&gt;ISMS (Information Security Management System)&lt;/strong&gt; and with certifications such as ISO27001, PCI-DSS, ISAE3402 SOC1, SOC2, etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to travel across our European locations (maximum 10% of time)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;IT or technical degree preferred. Degree in law is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong &lt;strong&gt;stakeholder management skills&lt;/strong&gt;, with the ability to engage at all levels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication skills and a &lt;strong&gt;people-focused cross stakeholder approach&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency in English.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Join Us?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead a high-impact role in a &lt;strong&gt;rapidly expanding digital infrastructure company&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape the &lt;strong&gt;future of operations&lt;/strong&gt; in emerging markets across Europe.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work in a dynamic, innovative environment with significant growth potential.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Join a company that values &lt;strong&gt;sustainability, efficiency, and cutting-edge solutions&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Apply now&lt;/strong&gt; and be part of our journey toward a more connected, efficient, and sustainable digital future.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Background Check &amp;amp; Screening&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;All selected candidates will undergo a background check to ensure a safe workplace, protect company assets, and comply with regulations.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Diversity &amp;amp; Inclusion Statement&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;br&gt;nLighten is an equal opportunity employer. We are committed to fostering an inclusive and diverse workplace, and we encourage applications from candidates of all backgrounds. Even if you do not meet every requirement listed, we welcome your application. We particularly encourage women and individuals from underrepresented groups to apply.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Buildkite&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Buildkite&#39;s CI platform is trusted by the world&#39;s leading engineering teams, helping ship software used by more than 1 billion people every day. Companies including Canva, Meta, Mistral AI, and NVIDIA rely on Buildkite to run builds, tests, and deployments on their infrastructure, ours, or both - giving them the speed, reliability, and flexibility to ship with confidence.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is not your average Support Engineer role. You&#39;ll support Buildkite&#39;s enterprise customers by independently troubleshooting and resolving highly complex CI/CD, software, and infrastructure problems, collaborating directly with Software Engineering teams at places like Canva, Uber, and Airbnb to help unblock critical workflows. You&#39;ll play a vital role in shaping the support team&#39;s evolution into a function that balances reactive and proactive work, spending half your time designing and implementing scalable tools, processes, and open source contributions that create a world-class customer experience. This role is a perfect opportunity for a Software, DevOps, or Infrastructure expert who is customer obsessed and thrives on solving tough technical problems for some of the world&#39;s most innovative engineering teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;This role is remote and requires someone to be located in the UK, Ireland or Poland. You&#39;ll work five days a week, 9:00 AM–5:00 PM local time, &lt;/em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;including both Saturday and Sunday&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;. Your other three days are flexible — we&#39;ll agree on a set schedule together when you join.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Independently resolve highly technical CI/CD, software, and infrastructure issues for enterprise customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide support through Slack, Zoom, Email, Plain, and Community Forum&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead customer-facing retrospectives and planning sessions to improve their Buildkite experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify opportunities to prevent future support issues and drive the design and implementation of proactive solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to and maintain open source tools such as Bash plugins and Golang-based utilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Publish documentation updates and proactive communications that improve the customer journey&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a voice for customers, ensuring their feedback shapes internal product and process improvements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and improve support workflows, simplifying how the team operates and delivers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Share learnings from customer work to strengthen alignment with Product and Engineering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor peers and foster an inclusive, supportive environment within the team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This Is You If You Have...&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Customer Centric Mindset&lt;/strong&gt; – Deep commitment to delivering world-class support with empathy and patience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Expertise&lt;/strong&gt; – Strong coding or scripting ability with experience in Bash, Ruby on Rails, or Golang&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;DevOps and Cloud Knowledge&lt;/strong&gt; – Solid experience with CI/CD tools and platforms including Linux, AWS, GCP, Azure, Terraform, and Kubernetes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Problem Solving Skills&lt;/strong&gt; – Confident in independently tackling complex technical issues and guiding customers to solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Autonomous and Proactive&lt;/strong&gt; – Able to work independently, identify opportunities early, and take initiative to drive meaningful improvements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Excellent Communication&lt;/strong&gt; – Skilled at articulating technical detail clearly to customers and internal teams across distributed environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;20 days paid annual leave plus 10 days sick &amp;amp; carer&#39;s leave&lt;/strong&gt; — actively encouraged, we want you to be at your best and time off is a part of that.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;An ongoing remote-work allowance to help you do your best work&lt;/strong&gt; — we want you to have everything you need, from great wifi to wellness options that are right for you.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Retirement and health coverage &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;(based on your region)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;— build towards your future, your way.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;16 weeks paid parental leave for primary carers (6 weeks for secondary)&lt;/strong&gt; — becoming a parent is life changing and we’re committed to supporting you and your family through it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Confidential EAP &amp;amp; mental health support&lt;/strong&gt; — sometimes life gets hard. You should be able to access the resources and support you need.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Support for learning and growth&lt;/strong&gt; — with time and budget for conferences, courses, and coaching so you have the opportunity to grow, improve your craft, and build mastery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Flexibility to work from anywhere in the world for up to 6 weeks a year&lt;/strong&gt; — great work doesn’t have to happen from one desk.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Exact benefits may vary slightly by country. We&#39;ll walk through the specifics for your location.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🌈 Equal Opportunity Employer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Buildkite, we value diversity and celebrate all types of skills, backgrounds, and experiences. We’re dedicated to fostering an inclusive environment and providing reasonable accommodations throughout our recruitment process.&lt;/p&gt;
