&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who We Are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Addepar is a global data and AI platform empowering investment professionals to turn complex financial information into actionable intelligence. Addepar unifies portfolio, market and client data in a total portfolio view and delivers AI-powered insights within investment and client workflows. More than 1,500 firms in 60 countries use Addepar to manage and advise on nearly $10 trillion in assets. Its open platform integrates with 650 software, data and consulting partners to power end-to-end investment operations across firms of all sizes and levels of complexity. Addepar supports clients worldwide with offices in New York City, Salt Lake City, São Paulo, London, Edinburgh, Geneva, Warsaw, Dubai, Pune and Singapore.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h4&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Precompute Platform team is seeking a Staff Engineer to join the team. The team is core to achieving Addepar&#39;s transition to using next generation tools and processes for data and analytics with a scalable global operating model. Its mission is to empower analysts, researchers, and other internal teams to performantly generate data and analytics artifacts. We operate on Terabyte-scale datasets, and enable second to sub-second performance by leveraging vector-oriented programming and distributed systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Applicants must have, and maintain, the right to work in the United Kingdom from the first day of employment. Please note that visa sponsorship is not available for this role.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Facilitate constructive, productive discussions around complex technical and organizational issues with a focus on solving business challenges.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Architect, implement, and maintain engineering solutions to solve sophisticated problems; write well-designed, testable code.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work in partnership with product managers and technology partners to plan &amp;amp; scope complex, long-term projects, including ones with external dependencies or multiple team members.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Gain foundational knowledge of core Addepar systems, including the Addepar Data Lakehouse. Use these insights to work with counterparts. Drive opportunities to improve the end-user experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reduce complexity through the adoption of strategic data architecture and workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Empower others to achieve a higher level of performance and help build a culture of lending support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;B.S., M.S., or Ph.D. in Computer Science or similar technical field (or equivalent practical experience).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in building and evolving large-scale, high-performing distributed systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years experience as a professional software engineer, primarily in Python.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with vector-oriented development (NumPy, PyArrow, Dask, Spark are preferred, but we are open to candidates with experience of other vector languages)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong AWS knowledge and architectural experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A confident and positive outlook with low ego; high degree of ingenuity, resourcefulness, and problem-solving skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Values&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Act Like an Owner - &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Think and operate with intention, purpose and care. Own outcomes.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build Together - &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Collaborate to unlock the best solutions. Deliver lasting value.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Champion Our Clients - &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Exceed client expectations. Our clients’ success is our success.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive Innovation - &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Be bold and unconstrained in problem solving. Transform the industry.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Embrace Learning - &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Engage our community to broaden our perspective. Bring a growth mindset.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;In addition to our core values, Addepar is proud to be an equal opportunity employer. We seek to bring together diverse ideas, experiences, skill sets, perspectives, backgrounds and identities to drive innovative solutions. We commit to promoting a welcoming environment where inclusion and belonging are held as a shared responsibility.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We will ensure that individuals with disabilities are provided reasonable accommodation to participate in the job application or interview process, to perform essential job functions, and to receive other benefits and privileges of employment. Please contact us to request accommodation.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;PHISHING SCAM WARNING: Addepar is among several companies recently made aware of a phishing scam involving con artists posing as hiring managers recruiting via email, text and social media. The imposters are creating misleading email accounts, conducting remote “interviews,” and making fake job offers in order to collect personal and financial information from unsuspecting individuals. Please be aware that no job offers will be made from Addepar without a formal interview process. Additionally, Addepar will not ask you to purchase equipment or supplies as part of your onboarding process. If you have any questions, please reach out to &lt;a ----------<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who We Are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Addepar is a global data and AI platform empowering investment professionals to turn complex financial information into actionable intelligence. Addepar unifies portfolio, market and client data in a total portfolio view and delivers AI-powered insights within investment and client workflows. More than 1,500 firms in 60 countries use Addepar to manage and advise on nearly $10 trillion in assets. Its open platform integrates with 650 software, data and consulting partners to power end-to-end investment operations across firms of all sizes and levels of complexity. Addepar supports clients worldwide with offices in New York City, Salt Lake City, São Paulo, London, Edinburgh, Geneva, Warsaw, Dubai, Pune and Singapore.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h4&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are currently seeking a Senior Full Stack Software Engineer to join our Feed &amp;amp; Workflow Intelligence team!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are part of a new initiative that seeks to leverage machine learning &amp;amp; artificial intelligence in order to accelerate the velocity of onboarding data (think everything from unstructured PDFs to complex CSV and Excel data sets) to the Addepar Data Lakehouse - Addepar’s proprietary system for managing data across the entire company. In this full-stack role, you’ll be part of a critical need to work directly on client-facing front-end and backend features that interact with our AI &amp;amp; ML powered backend and agentic file import platform to improve the experience of onboarding data globally.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Applicants must have, and maintain, the right to work in the United Kingdom from the first day of employment. Please note that visa sponsorship is not available for this role.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with product, design, engineering, and key clients to define and deliver&amp;nbsp; solutions that support and streamline user workflows aligned to Feed Intelligence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with our web platform and design system teams to ensure our product is a seamless part of the Addepar user experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement engineering solutions to address sophisticated problems; write well-designed, testable code.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bridge the gap between running and creating sophisticated AI &amp;amp; ML workflows with a seamless user experience for real client problems at Addepar&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s or Master’s degree in Computer Science or equivalent experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extensive full-stack development experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You care about delivering quality and value to clients in an agile manner&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Python and/or Java development experience on the backend side&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with agentic coding harnesses (Codex, Claude Code, OpenCode, etc.) is preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with React, web components, Svelte on the frontend side&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with AWS and associated datastores, such as Aurora RDS and DynamoDB&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building or using agentic systems, such as chat interfaces or running an agentic workflow, is a huge plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Values&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Act Like an Owner - &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Think and operate with intention, purpose and care. Own outcomes.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build Together - &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Collaborate to unlock the best solutions. Deliver lasting value.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Champion Our Clients - &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Exceed client expectations. Our clients’ success is our success.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive Innovation - &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Be bold and unconstrained in problem solving. Transform the industry.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Embrace Learning - &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Engage our community to broaden our perspective. Bring a growth mindset.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;In addition to our core values, Addepar is proud to be an equal opportunity employer. We seek to bring together diverse ideas, experiences, skill sets, perspectives, backgrounds and identities to drive innovative solutions. We commit to promoting a welcoming environment where inclusion and belonging are held as a shared responsibility.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We will ensure that individuals with disabilities are provided reasonable accommodation to participate in the job application or interview process, to perform essential job functions, and to receive other benefits and privileges of employment. Please contact us to request accommodation.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;PHISHING SCAM WARNING: Addepar is among several companies recently made aware of a phishing scam involving con artists posing as hiring managers recruiting via email, text and social media. The imposters are creating misleading email accounts, conducting remote “interviews,” and making fake job offers in order to collect personal and financial information from unsuspecting individuals. Please be aware that no job offers will be made from Addepar without a formal interview process. Additionally, Addepar will not ask you to purchase equipment or supplies as part of your onboarding process. If you have any questions, please reach out to &lt;a ----------<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;h4&gt;About Team &amp;amp; About Role&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Rubrik&#39;s Alliances team works with the world&#39;s leading systems integrators to help hospitals, banks, governments and other critical organisations across EMEA keep operating through cyberattacks. As Director, GSI Alliances EMEA, you&#39;ll build and lead the regional GSI strategy from the ground up, turning partnerships with the biggest integrators into a repeatable engine for pipeline, services and cyber resilience outcomes. This is a rare chance to shape how Rubrik goes to market through GSIs across a whole region, with real ownership of the strategy and the team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and own Rubrik&#39;s EMEA GSI strategy, deciding which partners to prioritise and where to invest, so Rubrik is the data security platform integrators lead with in customer resilience programmes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build executive-level relationships with the regional and global leadership of our priority GSIs, creating joint plans that turn partnership into sourced and influenced pipeline&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Sales, Pre-Sales, Marketing and Specialist sales teams to align GSI engagement to key accounts, so customers get a joined-up Rubrik and partner experience from first conversation to deployment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and scale GSI service offerings, certifications and practices around Rubrik&#39;s platform, including data security, cyber recovery and identity resilience, so more customers can adopt faster with trusted delivery partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hire, coach and develop a high-performing GSI alliances team, creating clear paths for people to grow as the region scales&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the GSI forecast, business plans and quarterly reviews, using data to show what&#39;s working and where to double down&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent Rubrik at partner events, customer briefings and industry forums, shaping how the market sees us in regulated sectors such as financial services, public sector and healthcare&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with global Alliances and Product leadership to bring EMEA partner and customer insight into roadmap, programme and incentive decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Experience You&#39;ll Need&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Substantial experience in alliances, partnerships or channel leadership within enterprise software, ideally cybersecurity, data protection, cloud or infrastructure, with a strong track record working with GSIs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated success building GSI relationships at senior level and turning them into measurable pipeline and revenue&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading and developing teams, or leading through influence across Sales, Marketing and Services without direct authority&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of how GSIs make money (services attach, managed services, practice build-outs) and how to build joint value propositions around that&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to build and execute a regional strategy across multiple countries, cultures and regulatory environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and executive presence, comfortable with CxO-level conversations in both partner and customer settings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commercial discipline: you plan, forecast and report with rigour&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building a GSI or alliances function in a high-growth or scaling company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with EMEA regulatory drivers such as DORA and NIS2 and how they shape cyber resilience buying&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Existing relationships with major GSIs and regional integrators across EMEA&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Additional European languages&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with marketplace and co-sell motions across the major hyperscalers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Join Us in Securing and Accelerating the World&#39;s AI Transformation&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Rubrik (NYSE: RBRK) is the Security and AI Operations Company, delivering one platform built at the intersection of data, identity, and AI. The platform enables agentic cyber resilience and trusted AI operations for enterprises worldwide, built to recover before disruption strikes and stay a step ahead, so security is never the reason ambition stalls.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/company/rubrik-inc/mycompany/verification/&quot;&gt;Linkedin&lt;/a&gt; | &lt;a href=&quot;https://twitter.com/rubrikinc&quot;&gt;X (formerly Twitter)&lt;/a&gt; | &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.instagram.com/rubrikinc/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Instagram&lt;/a&gt; |&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.rubrik.com&quot;&gt;Rubrik.com&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Inclusion @ Rubrik&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Rubrik, we are dedicated to fostering a culture where people from all backgrounds are valued, feel they belong, and believe they can succeed. Our commitment to inclusion is at the heart of our mission to secure the world’s data.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our goal is to hire and promote the best talent, regardless of background. We continually review our hiring practices to ensure fairness and strive to create an environment where every employee has equal access to opportunities for growth and excellence. We believe in empowering everyone to bring their authentic selves to work and achieve their fullest potential.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Our inclusion strategy focuses on three core areas of our business and culture:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1;&quot;&gt;Our Company: We are committed to building a merit-based organization that offers equal access to growth and success for all employees globally. Your potential is limitless here.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1;&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our Culture: We strive to create an inclusive atmosphere where individuals from all backgrounds feel a strong sense of belonging, can thrive, and do their best work. Your contributions help us innovate and break boundaries.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1;&quot;&gt;Our Communities: We are dedicated to expanding our engagement with the communities we operate in, creating opportunities for underrepresented talent and driving greater innovation for our clients. Your impact extends beyond Rubrik, contributing to safer and stronger communities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Equal Opportunity Employer/Veterans/Disabled&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Rubrik is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, disability, genetic information, protected veteran status, or any other status protected by applicable law. Rubrik provides equal employment opportunities to employees and applicants in all terms and conditions of employment, including recruiting, hiring, promotion, compensation, training, leave, and termination.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Rubrik provides reasonable accommodations to qualified applicants and employees with disabilities in accordance with applicable law. If you need an accommodation to participate in the application process or to perform your job, please contact&amp;nbsp;&lt;a ----- ----- Accommodations may include changes to the application process, documents in an alternate format, a sign language interpreter, or specialized equipment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.eeoc.gov/sites/default/files/2023-06/22-088_EEOC_KnowYourRights6.12ScreenRdr.pdf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;EEO IS THE LAW&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.dol.gov/sites/dolgov/files/olms/regs/compliance/eo_posters/employeerightsposter2page_19final.pdf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;NOTIFICATION OF EMPLOYEE RIGHTS UNDER FEDERAL LABOR LAWS&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;Pantheon has been at the forefront of private markets investing for more than 40 years, earning a reputation for an innovative approach to investing in secondaries, co-investments, and primary fund investments, as well as capital formation across commingled funds, evergreen vehicles and customized solutions. Our specialist investment capabilities span multiple strategies across private equity, infrastructure and real assets, and private credit. Through our collaborative and committed culture, we find new ways to solve complex problems together and deliver innovative investment opportunities across private markets. Pantheon currently manages approximately $82.3 billion in AUM across all its strategies, serving more than 750 institutional and 638 private wealth clients worldwide&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For further details please visit &lt;a href=&quot;http://www.pantheon.com&quot;&gt;www.pantheon.com&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Purpose of Position&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Product Manager / Deal Lead within the Global Insurance Structured Solutions team, within the Client Solutions Group.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Role will work in close partnership with colleagues across the business, including the investment teams and global relationship managers, to develop, commercialise and execute new structured solutions and other products for insurers, asset managers, banks and others. The Role will also work with external parties within the insurance, asset management and structured solutions world, such as advisors, law firms, rating agencies, distributors, investors, brokers, regulators and others (“External Parties”), to create partnerships, appoint service providers, maintain market intelligence and know-how and develop new products and solutions for the business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The role will encompass several key areas (further and more complete details below):&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Product management “Deal Lead”&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ongoing management and servicing of existing products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;New Product development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Counterparty Relationship coverage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Investor-facing/RM support&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;GISS team strategy and agenda&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Product management “Deal Lead”: leading structuring and management of launch process for new structured, insurance and other solutions (RFs, CFOs, bilateral CFOs, long-dated bonds, synthetic LPs etc, “Solutions”), in close coordination with Internal and External Parties, and managing more junior GISS colleagues involved in the product launch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ongoing management and servicing of existing Solutions: ongoing servicing of existing Solutions and support of investors, Relationship Managers and internal product management teams (CorePM, Fund Finance etc), for example, (i) developing the quarterly CFO monitoring and product management process in partnership with CorePM, Risk, Operations and Fund Finance, (ii) producing materials for investor meetings or other internal and external meetings and/or (iii) responding to internal or external questions about our business, services and Solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;New Product Development – the research and development of new solutions and products. This will often be an iterative process involving ideation and development with External Parties (in any location) as well as internal colleagues such as other team members, investment teams, CSG colleagues, legal, operations, tax, compliance, CorePM and others (“Internal Parties”).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Counterparty Relationship coverage — maintaining and expanding our existing network across advisors, investors, distributors, rating agencies, law firms and other External Parties, including regular in-person meetings, informal market contact, conferences and other engagements (for the benefit of Solutions and investors in all locations).
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Taking primary responsibility for relationships with External Parties where assigned to the Role, but also involving other team members involved in those relationships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintaining involvement in relationships with External Parties where responsibility is assigned to another team member&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Involvement of other GISS team members in such meetings and interactions for the benefit of the learning, development and relationship development of other team members, as well as for the purposes of innovation/ideation of new Solutions and projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Gather and aggregate market information, know-how, client needs, regulatory regimes, etc to help development of new ideas and to support execution of new solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Investor-facing/RM support — supporting RMs at investor pitches and marketing meetings (both in person and remotely) as well as with ongoing relationship servicing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;GISS team strategy and agenda.
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supporting the team head and the wider global GISS team, preserving global collaboration across the group.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Representing the interests of the GISS team and the business as a leader within the GISS team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Managing junior team members, either direct reports, or other more junior team members who are not direct reports but with whom the Role is working on Solutions and projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate closely with the head of the GISS team, other Product Managers / Deal Leads and the broader GISS team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Note that responsibilities will need to be flexible to meet the needs of the GISS team, our stakeholders and the business more broadly, so these will likely evolve over time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Knowledge and Experience Required&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Significant experience in product development/management, investment solutions structuring and/or insurance solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience of private markets, including secondaries, and across private credit, private equity, infrastructure and other private assets, and ideally also good knowledge of public debt markets, risk factors and dynamics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with securitisations, collateralised fund obligations (“CFOs”) and rated feeder structures, including rating methodologies, modelling, structuring, investors, regulatory treatment, and other topics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Existing relationships with market participants including rating agencies, lawyers, brokers, investors, asset managers and/or regulators.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong project management and organisational skills with demonstrated aptitude for prioritisation and execution of complex projects and assigning and hitting deadlines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of global insurance regulatory environments and the implications for both investment portfolio requirements and vehicle structures, including how to optimise for various client needs, especially capital treatment efficiency, liquidity and other objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing more junior staff&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Legal knowledge/understanding and experience an advantage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication skills, both written and verbal.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong problem-solving skills and ability to work well in a team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This job description is not to be construed as an exhaustive statement of duties, responsibilities, or requirements. You may be required to perform other job-related duties as reasonably requested by your manager.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pantheon is an Equal Opportunities employer, we are committed to building a diverse and inclusive workforce so if you&#39;re excited about this role but your past experience doesn&#39;t perfectly align we&#39;d still encourage you to apply.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Flexport:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Flexport, we believe global trade can move the human race forward. That’s why it’s our mission to make global commerce so easy there will be more of it. We’re shaping the future of a $10T industry with solutions powered by innovative technology and exceptional people. Today, companies of all sizes—from emerging brands to Fortune 500s—use Flexport technology to move more than $19B of merchandise across 112 countries a year.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The recent global supply chain crisis has put Flexport center stage as we continue to play a pivotal role in how goods move around the world. We are proud to have the support of the best investors in the game who believe in our mission, solutions and people. Ready to tackle global challenges that impact business, society, and the environment? Come join us.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Please submit your CV in English!&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The opportunity:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The role of the Operations Associate is a critical part of making Flexport’s mission to make global trade easy for everyone a reality. Flexport today connects almost 10,000 clients and suppliers across 109 countries. In this role, your direct customers are the partners within your region: our account management and customs teams, subcontractors, carriers, terminals and trucking providers. Your work directly supports Flexport’s end customers in achieving their logistics goals. Most importantly, you will play a pivotal role in building the next operational model at Flexport: allowing us to effectively scale to achieve our mission of making global trade easier for everyone.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is designed to facilitate the movement of shipments while discovering and driving efficiencies that build and improve operations as part of our Global team. You will be responsible for ensuring that all customer shipments are executed according to plan, on time and within budget. As the person who manages movement in your region with laser focus, you have the unique opportunity to help your regional account team spot opportunities to improve and grow our customers’ business. You will drive impact through surfacing new ideas to eliminate waste, improve customer experience or introducing innovative ways of managing a supply chain.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be the “front line” in ensuring the highest standard of Flexport quality: shipments move on-time and exceptions are handled appropriately&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be responsible for ensuring your work satisfies internal KPIs and SLAs that demonstrate quality delivery&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Follow standard operating procedures (SOP)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solve client issues quickly and ensure smooth operations at origin and destination and escalate issues as needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Acting in the best interest of the company by avoiding leakages and ensuring cost conscious behavior&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Seamlessly coordinate day-to-day logistics operations with internal and external partners such as steamship lines, air carriers, intermodal and drayage vendors, customs, trade lane management, warehousing, transloading, trucking, and the air operations team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execute the end-to-end movement of freight shipments within a regional network (both imports and exports), including intermodal movements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist the shipments managed by partners as we drive partner autonomy (if applicable in a given region)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Prerequisites:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;BA/BS Degree or completed professional training as forwarding agent&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: bold;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;3+ years of experience in freight forwarding, and direct Air export experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Fluent in French and English&lt;/strong&gt; (other European languages are a plus)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to adapt to new technology and can thrive in a fast paced environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Effective time management, be able to properly prioritize and manage a large volume of tasks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Attention to detail&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to effectively seek and receive feedback&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Effective communication both verbally and in writing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Teamwork and relationship building&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Orientation towards working smarter and adopting best practices and standardization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Problem-solving capabilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A “compliance first” attitude to keep our regulators happy and enthusiastic about Flexport since we operate in a heavily regulated industry&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What else:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You will work in a beautiful office in the city center of Paris with modern office equipment and a first class connection to the public transport system of Paris.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You will work in a fast growing and changing environment with a high motivated team, which is always open to hear your ideas&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We invest in your personal and professional development by offering you internal and external trainings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;During regular team events you can have a lot of fun with your teammates and connect with them aside from your working day&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we offer:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An opportunity to contribute to one of the fastest-growing companies, where you’ll have the chance to create a global impact while being a part of a&amp;nbsp; thriving multinational environment&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;25 working days&lt;/strong&gt; working days of paid annual leave per complete year of service&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The employee shall be affiliated to the French social security system (Sécurité sociale) and the mandatory supplementary pension schemes (retraite complémentaire AGIRC-ARRCO) in accordance with applicable law. Employer and employee contributions shall be calculated and deducted in accordance with statutory rates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;50% reimbursement of the cost of the public transportation subscription(s) used for travel between your place of residence and the workplace.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Employer&#39;s collective supplementary health insurance scheme (mutuelle d&#39;entreprise) as required by law. Flexport shall contribute at least 50% of the premium for the base coverage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lunches compensation&lt;/strong&gt;: EUR 12 for every day worked in the office&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Parental leave benefit:&lt;/strong&gt; Flexport is here to support you and your families in one of the most important times in life – the birth of a child! Our parental leave program allows both mothers and partners to take time off from work for pregnancy, childbirth, and to bond with your new child.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Equity program: every team member becomes a shareholder, aligning our success with yours. As a private company in a multi-trillion dollar industry, you have a direct stake in our collective growth and success.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#LI-onsite&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;#LI-BG1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
